Product Requirement & Technical Architecture Document: Parivahan ExpressProject Name: Parivahan ExpressTarget Platform: Parivahan Sewa (Learner's Licence & Driving Licence Services)Document Purpose: Complete Technical & Product Specification for AI Coding Agents and Development Teams1. Executive Summary & Core ObjectiveParivahan Express is a zero-failure, mobile-first web interface designed to sit in front of public driving licence portals. It eliminates the primary bottlenecks that force citizens to rely on paid cybercafés: rigid image upload constraints, session data loss on patchy mobile networks, cryptic validation error codes, and field format confusion.The platform operates entirely client-side, using browser-native storage and HTML5 APIs to handle document editing, data persistence, and pre-flight validation before any payload touches the server.2. System Architecture & Technology SelectionSelected ArchitectureArchitecture Type: Client-Side Single Page Application (SPA) / Progressive Web App (PWA)Core Technology Stack: Vanilla ES6+ JavaScript, Native Web APIs (IndexedDB, HTML5 Canvas API, Web Speech API), Tailwind CSS framework.Tech Stack RationaleZero Framework Overhead: Avoiding heavy frameworks (React, Vue, Angular) ensures the bundle size stays below 30 KB gzipped. This guarantees instant loading on 2G/3G mobile networks and low-end smartphones.Native Browser Capability: Using native IndexedDB and Canvas APIs allows processing images and storing application state directly on the user's hardware without relying on external cloud processing APIs or server queues.Static Hosting Feasibility: The entire application can be deployed on static hosting infrastructure (Vercel, GitHub Pages) without maintaining an active application server layer.3. Application Workflow & Page StructureThe application consists of two main views:View 1: Landing & Orientation PageHeader Banner: Attribution pill displaying: Built for India | High-Resilience Civic Portal Prototype.Hero Section: Clear value proposition highlighting zero data loss, offline capability, and automatic document resizing.Primary Action: Single high-contrast button (Start DL / LL Application) routing to the main form view.Feature Highlights Grid: Three visual cards detailing the Inline Media Studio, Offline Resilience, and Pre-Flight Validation system.View 2: Application & Media Studio PortalHeader Bar: Platform title, back button, and a real-time network status pill (Online / Offline Caching Active).Visual Progress Tracker: 3-step indicator (1. Personal Details $\rightarrow$ 2. Document Studio $\rightarrow$ 3. Pre-Flight Verification).Form Area: Single-column touch-friendly input form with inline guidance drawers, file upload croppers, and an auto-save status indicator.4. Form Field Specifications & Validation RulesField Group 1: Identity & State InformationField NameInput TypeValidation RulesHelp / Guidance Drawer ContentState SelectionDropdownRequired. Must match a valid Indian State/UT.Select the state matching your permanent address proof.RTO OfficeDropdownRequired. Populates based on selected state.Choose the RTO location closest to your permanent address.Full NameTextRequired. 3 to 50 characters. Letters and spaces only.Enter your full name exactly as printed on your official identity document.Date of BirthText / DateRequired. Must follow DD/MM/YYYY format. Age must be $\ge 16$ for LL or $\ge 18$ for DL.Format: DD/MM/YYYY. Enter your birth date as registered in educational or identity records.Licence / Application No.TextOptional for new applicants; Required for renewals/transfers. Must match state regex patterns.Where to find this? Search your mobile SMS inbox for sender IDs like PARIVN or AD-PARIVN containing keywords "Application Number" or "DL".Field Group 2: Document Studio UploadsUpload CategoryFormat ConstraintsTarget Dimensions & SizeClient-Side Auto-Processing BehaviorApplicant PhotoJPG / JPEGTarget Size: $\le 20\text{ KB}$Aspect Ratio: $3:4$ (Passport style)Triggers Inline Media Studio. Auto-crops aspect ratio, boosts contrast for low-light photos, and applies iterative compression to strictly hit $\le 20\text{ KB}$.Signature UploadJPG / JPEGTarget Size: $\le 10\text{ KB}$Aspect Ratio: $3:1$Converts background to high-contrast monochrome (white background, dark ink) and compresses binary payload to $\le 10\text{ KB}$.5. Detailed Feature SpecificationsFeature 1: Inline Media Studio (Canvas-Based Processing)Problem Solved: Government upload forms fail if images exceed arbitrary size limits (e.g., $20\text{ KB}$), forcing users to visit external compression websites or pay cybercafé operators.Functional Logic:When a user selects or takes a photo, an embedded canvas modal opens over the current screen.The user can drag and pinch to adjust the crop frame (enforcing official aspect ratios).An automatic contrast algorithm analyzes the image pixels: if dark or uneven, it adjusts contrast and brightness levels to ensure clear facial recognition and signature visibility.The compression engine runs a binary search on the image output quality rating until the resulting byte size is strictly equal to or under the target threshold ($20\text{ KB}$ for photos, $10\text{ KB}$ for signatures).The processed file is attached to the form payload without changing pages.Feature 2: Zero-Loss Offline Engine (IndexedDB)Problem Solved: Poor mobile network connections or accidental page refreshes wipe form entries, forcing users to restart long applications.Functional Logic:The application initializes a local browser database named ParivahanExpressDB with an object store application_drafts.Every input field listens for user edits. A debounced auto-save triggers 200 milliseconds after typing stops, writing the entire form state to IndexedDB.Uploaded image binaries are stored locally as Blobs alongside text inputs.When the page reloads or the connection drops, the app checks IndexedDB and instantly restores all text fields, select dropdowns, and cropped images.A subtle floating badge confirms: "Draft saved to your device".Feature 3: Client-Side Error Interceptor & DictionaryProblem Solved: Raw system error codes (e.g., ERR_STATE_FORMAT_404) confuse users and offer no actionable path forward.Functional Logic:An error dictionary layer evaluates validation failures against human-readable remediation entries:Licence Format Error: Maps raw format errors to clean instructions: "Your DL number must start with your 2-letter state code followed by a 4-digit year (e.g., RJ-14-2022-XXXXXXX)."Date of Birth Mismatch: Explains exact date formatting rules and age eligibility thresholds.Network Timeout: Reassures the user that their data is safely cached on their phone and will automatically submit once connectivity returns.Error alerts display clear titles, simple explanations, and step-by-step resolution actions.Feature 4: Pre-Flight Verification & Readiness ScoringProblem Solved: Users submit incomplete or incorrectly formatted applications, leading to rejection fees and delayed processing.Functional Logic:Before allowing final submission, the platform opens a Pre-Flight Summary Modal.The system computes an Application Readiness Score (0% to 100%) based on:Required field completeness ($40\%$).Valid format verification across state and date fields ($20\%$).Photo crop and byte size compliance ($20\%$).Signature contrast and byte size compliance ($20\%$).The modal displays a visual summary card showing the cropped photo, enhanced signature, state choices, and RTO location for final user confirmation.6. Visual Design System & UX StandardsColor Palette (Civic Dark Palette)Primary Background: Slate Dark #0F172ACard & Surface Background: Slate Navy #1E293BCard Borders & Dividers: Muted Slate #334155Primary Brand / Action Accent: Emerald #059669 (Hover/Active State: #047857)Warnings & Hints: Amber #D97706Primary Text: White #F8FAFCSecondary / Hint Text: Cool Slate #94A3B8Typography & Spacing GuidelinesFont Family: System Font Stack (Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, sans-serif).Touch Optimization: All form inputs, buttons, select boxes, and modal triggers must have a minimum height of 48px to ensure effortless operation on mobile touchscreens.Single Column Layout: The main form follows a centered, single-column design pattern on screens below 768px width to prevent horizontal scrolling.
